I'm happy to say that last night, my rogue Wiggum became my second 
character to ascend to demigod status.

I completed my first ascension, Miss Hoover the valkyrie, after roughly 
2 years of playing.  As I was pretty spoiled almost from the beginning, 
I assumed it would be many months, though hopefully less than 2 years, 
before I ascended again.  But happily, it took less than 3 months (5 
weeks of which was spent on this game), and only(?) 77 characters, to 
ascend Wiggum.  (This is compared to >400 characters on this computer 
before my first ascension, and probably at least as many on another 
machine.)

So I'm curious - how long do people typically take for their *second* 
ascension?

Here are the highlights from Wiggum's game:

* Wiggum (rog-hum-mal-cha) began play around the end of April and 
ascended on June 1.  I'd never had any success with rogues previously, 
but was intrigued by a thread about rogue strategy shortly after my 
first ascension, and I played mostly rogues since then.  They're 
different enough from the combat wombats I usually play - I found I was 
actually bored when I tried to play a couple barbarians - though Wiggum 
was so overprepared for Gehennom that I did revert back to that style by 
the late game.

* Early game yielded speed boots, a +5 dwarvish helmet, a random 
Demonbane, and 2 /oPoly.

* I got the "oR from Sokoban, which I usually don't like, but I didn't 
mind this time, since I started with the sack.  In hindsight, this was 
probably a key factor to my success.

* Smoky potions were gain energy, and I got a wish from one after 
Sokoban.  After long deliberation, I chose a [CoMR, over a (BoH or "oLS.  
Again in hindsight, I think this was a very good call.

* A sacrifest in mine town yielded Orcrist and Trollsbane.  Yeah.  I 
returned later in the game and sacrificed for Werebane.  Woo-hoo. :|

* I summoned Yeenoghu at the altar, who I somehow managed to not 
accidentally attack until much later.  Happily, I was able to kill him 
at that point, and surprisingly much more easily than I expected to.

* I was a moron on the quest, blowing up a bag of holding, and trapping 
myself for tens of thousands of turns, having to live on my =oSD and 
leprechaun meat.  I also trapped myself for long periods between Medusa 
and the castle, and between the castle and Jubilex.  Hence an extremely 
high turn count.

* I also can't have a good game without a polymorph accident.  Happily, 
I only lost a Hawaiian shirt.  And while I prefer a stylish Hawaiian 
shirt, I had an equally effective t-shirt ("Yendor Military Soldiers Do 
It In Large Groups") in my stash.

* The castle /oW only had 1 charge, but I only used 5 wishes the entire 
game – 3 from smoky potions, 2 from the wand.

* Orcus Town was cool.  I found a random /oDeath shortly before I killed 
Orcus for his.  Then while passing back through on my ascension run, a 
jabberwock dropped a /oW with 2 charges (though I never used it).

* The altar in mine town was the ONLY one in the game before the Valley 
of the Dead.  Not a single random altar in the entire game!

* I also didn't find any of the following "nice to have" items randomly 
until Gehennom: tinning kit, stethescope, shirt, magic whistle, magic 
lamp.  Even extensive polypiling (about 10-12 charges on a pile with 
dozens of tools, including some unihorns and other magical tools) failed 
to produce a magic whistle.  I like to travel with pets, but I just gave 
up this game.  I finally found a magic whistle on level 35, but didn't 
tame any pets again until my ascension run, when I wished up a second 
silver dagger to replace Stormbringer.

* As a rogue, I collected all valuables (amulets, artifacts, and gems) 
to ascend with.  I decided against killing the Priest of Moloch in the 
VotD and lugging all the gold I'd donated up to Astral though.

* Rodney only reappeared twice on the ascension run.  He never left a 
corpse, so my quest to ascend with a tin of Wizard of Yendor meat will 
have to continue.

* Famine was on the left, Death in the middle, Pestilence on the right.  
Famine was easy last time, so I went left, but the altar was Mog's.  
Pestilence was not easy last time, so I went center to face Death, and 
this altar was to Kos.  I wanted to ascend with a full complement of 9 
pets, so I tamed a bunch of monsters around me, mounted Ralph the Red 
Dragon, whistled all my pets, and #offered the amulet.  For some reason, 
though, only 7 came with me.  Can anyone tell me why this happened?  1 
pet got left behind last time I ascended too.  Could they have been 
eating?  I didn't get a message to that effect, though I'm not sure 
you'd get that message when ascending.

* I only used 5 wishes (I used 14 my first time!): [CoMR (smoky potion, 
after Sokoban), [SDSM (smoky potion, after the castle), [HoTelepathy 
(castle wand, before Gehennom) a silver dagger (castle wand, before 
ascension run), and I think the fifth may have been a magic marker 
(smoky potion, not sure when).  I ascended with 3 total charges left in 
the castle wand, 6 total charges left in the Orcus Town /oW, and a magic 
lamp.



